WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Binary-only: picinfo is an uninstrumented Linux ELF with a planted NULL read. Reading it without running it shows its architecture, its imports, and that it opens a file.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Seeds can come from the model: describe the input in one line and it drafts candidates from the binary's strings and imports (1.5x).

3
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.800
Waiting for the model (sped up 20x).

4
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:46.800
Eight proposed seeds, shown before anything is used. The dictionary below comes from the binary's strings.

5
00:00:46.800 --> 00:01:01.800
Comparison splitting (CompCov) is on by default. Persistent mode loops on main inside one emulated process instead of starting one per input.

6
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.100
One minute in the sandbox (sped up 10x). The live panel shows executions, crashes and stability.

7
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:34.100
420,504 executions at 7,008 per second with 100% stability; the two earlier sessions in the history, from before persistent mode, ran 215,529 and 157,418. One distinct SEGV, confirmed by replay in a fresh process.

8
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:47.100
Stack frames as module offsets.

9
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:53.100
The model explains the crash from the replay, the input and the disassembly around the fault (sped up 4x).

10
00:01:53.100 --> 00:02:18.100
It names the faulting load, ldrb w2, [x22, x0], and the input byte that zeroes x22. The disassembly sent with the request is shown under the note.

11
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:41.100
Binary sessions are also listed in Triage, with their findings.
